      "message": "Does this have the potential to create an SA that is exactly identical to another SA, including having the same mark? Example:\n\n1. Create SA A with mark 1234/0xffffffff.\n2. Create identical SA B with mark 0/0.\n3. Update SA A to have mark 1234/0xffffffff.\n\nThat seems like a problem.\n\nIf the sequence above doesn\u0027t cause the problem, then I suspect that a situation where there are two threads racing to update the two SAs will still result in a duplicate.",
